{{!
    @template theme_nit/navbar_mode_toggle

    The navbar light/dark switch. Rendered by
    theme_nit\output\core_renderer::navbar_mode_toggle().

    Each mode maps to a Brand-Colors group (assigned on the gallery
    "Change style" tab → "Site styles"); the click handler swaps that group's
    switch class on <html>, so the page re-skins with no reload. `data-nit-mode`
    holds the mode currently showing — CSS keys the icon off it, so the button
    shows a moon in light mode and a sun in dark, i.e. the mode it switches TO.

    Both icons are in the markup and CSS hides the one that does not apply,
    rather than JavaScript rewriting the glyph: the icon then follows the
    attribute the handler already sets, and the server-rendered first paint is
    correct with no script at all.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * mode - the mode currently showing, "light" or "dark"
    * label - accessible name: the mode the button switches TO
    * config - JSON for the click handler ({classes, labels, cookie, path, secure})

    Example context (json):
    {
        "mode": "light",
        "label": "Switch to dark mode",
        "config": "{\"classes\":{\"light\":\"nit-mode-light\",\"dark\":\"nit-mode-dark nit-brand-2\"}}"
    }
}}
<button type="button" class="btn nit-navbar-icon nit-mode-toggle"
        data-nit-mode-toggle data-nit-mode="{{mode}}" data-nit-mode-config="{{config}}"
        title="{{label}}" aria-label="{{label}}">
    <i class="icon fa fa-moon fa-fw nit-mode-icon nit-mode-icon-dark m-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    <i class="icon fa fa-sun fa-fw nit-mode-icon nit-mode-icon-light m-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    <span class="visually-hidden nit-mode-toggle-label">{{label}}</span>
</button>
